  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nAn upper ridge over the western states will build into Montana \nthis week with temperatures warming into Friday. Look for highs \nFriday to reach the 90s north to the low 100s south. West winds \nwill also increase as a surface low passes east to the northeast \nof us. It looks like fuels will quickly dry and will be \nsusceptible to burn, therefore a Fire Weather Watch was issued for\nFriday.\n\nA Excessive Heat Watch was issued for Friday through Sunday as\nnighttime lows will also not be cool enough for recovery for\nsensitive people.\n\nSomewhat lighter winds are expected Saturday but slightly lower\nhumidities will keep the Fire Weather concerns alive.\n\nSlightly cooler conditions are expected Sunday but not enough to\nremove the Fire Weather concerns. \n\nLighter winds and higher humidity, especially in the northeast\nzones should continue to hack away at the Fire Weather concerns\nMonday.\n\nOtherwise, scattered thunderstorms over Canada and southern\nMontana shouldn't generally affect the area through the weekend.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nGoing NBM forecast generally good. Concerned that increasing smoke\naloft could suppress temperatures through the week. While have not\nadjusted temperatures, have begun to add haze into the forecast.\nTFJ",
